                                 <tr>
                                 <h2 style="color:#7b412b; font-weight: bold; font-size:14px; padding-top: 1.5%;" >4. Technology Absorption</h2>
                                 </tr>
								 
								 <ul style="color:#333; padding-left: 2.2%;">
								  <li>The state of the art technology for Paste fill plant at MCP underground mine has been planned after successful test work carried out by M/s  M/s Golder Associate- the technology supplier. This technology will be implemented for filling the void by utilising mine waste. This will ensure better waste management and sustainable mining.</li>

<li>The software based technology for 3D Ore body modelling and Mine planning is being implemented across all the mining Units. </li>

<li>Procurement of a new technology based total station survey instrument for mine surveying operation at MCP is under process. This is a target-less laser-based survey instrument and it also uses the latest windows operating system.</li>

<li>A study has been conducted to establish a suitable system for communication and auto-signalling at MCP underground mine and procurement of suitable communication system is under process.</li>

<li>IIT, Kharagpur is conducting stability analysis at Banwas block of Khetri Copper Mine. Recommendations shall help in designing safer stopes while also increasing extraction at Banwas block.</li>

<li>NIRM(National Institute of Rock Mechanics) has been appointed for carrying out geo-technical modelling for the entire open pit and the Underground mine at MCP. The study will help in analysing the risk in respect of stability of rock structure(open pit & underground mine) and mitigation plan if any. This will help in ensuring safe and sustainable mining in underground mines.</li>
</ul>
